  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The `perfPowerMetricsresource` resource is a read-only resource where you get the power and performance metrics and diagnostics for App Store versions of your app. Use this information to improve your app’s performance. Customers can opt-in to share this information with you on their devices.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A *metric* is a measurement of the power and performance impact of an app running on a device. The `MetricCategory` type lists the categories of measurements the system makes; for example, the `LAUNCH` metric measures how long it takes an app to present its first frame. Use the `GET-v1-apps-_id_-perfPowerMetrics` and `GET-v1-builds-_id_-perfPowerMetrics` endpoints to get the metrics reports for the most recent version of your app or for a specific build.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreconnectapi/documentation/AppStoreConnectAPI/MetricCategory",
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreconnectapi/documentation/AppStoreConnectAPI/GET-v1-apps-_id_-perfPowerMetrics",
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreconnectapi/documentation/AppStoreConnectAPI/GET-v1-builds-_id_-perfPowerMetrics"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "An *insight* is an automatically generated analysis that shows a trend based on a set of metrics data. Insights compare the performance of the most recent app version with previous versions. Look for insights in the response body object, `xcodeMetrics`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreconnectapi/documentation/AppStoreConnectAPI/xcodeMetrics"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A *diagnostic signature* is a recurring pattern of function calls your app makes that are associated with a metric. To get a diagnostic log for a signature, first call the `GET-v1-builds-_id_-diagnosticSignatures` endpoint to get the resource IDs for signatures you’re interested in. Then call `GET-v1-diagnosticSignatures-_id_-logs` using the signature resource IDs to download the logs.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreconnectapi/documentation/AppStoreConnectAPI/GET-v1-builds-_id_-diagnosticSignatures",
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreconnectapi/documentation/AppStoreConnectAPI/GET-v1-diagnosticSignatures-_id_-logs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To learn more about power and performance metrics, see `https://help.apple.com/xcode/mac/current/#/devb642b28ac`, and `Improving Your App's Performance`.",
          "refs": [
            "https://help.apple.com/xcode/mac/current/#/devb642b28ac"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    }
  ],
